{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"document database document database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md","fileName":"Document Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Document Database","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Azure Cosmos DB Applications]] [[Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Cosmos DB Applications","Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"document database document database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md","fileName":"Document Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Document Database","heading":"Document Database","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A document database stores records as self-describing documents rather than rows constrained to one relational table shape. Documents can contain the fields needed for an application object and are commonly addressed through a collection and a unique identifier.\n\nThe book presents Cosmos DB as the successor branding for Microsoft's DocumentDB service and accesses work-item documents through a MongoDB-compatible API. Document flexibility does not remove the need for deliberate identifiers, query patterns, and capacity planning.\n\nEmbedding related information in one document can reduce cross-record coordination, while relationships that require independent updates or broad joins may remain a better fit for another data model.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Cosmos DB Applications","Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"document database document database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Document Database.md","fileName":"Document Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Document Database","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n[[hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Cosmos DB Applications","Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}